  "section_notes": "The final S2 requires 55 °C testing and gives customers numeric per-model rates but bars public publication, and a failure rate above 5% triggers only a corrective-action plan, so no sales stop applies; this is the main benefit to Northwind. S3 allows a 6-year retrofit window (acceptable, not safe), matching Northwind's red line, while S4 delays built-in suppression to 36 months, matching Halcyon's red line. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition or corrective alternative, which is strict on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) but leaves Hearth 10 (6.4) clear. The 'scope' and 'customer notice' conversions use 5 business days = 7 calendar days."
